ocratic win at 12%"], "rationale": "The district's R+10 lean, Schmidt's incumbency and clear fundraising edge, and a unanimous expert consensus at Safe or Solid R all point to a comfortable Republican margin. Polymarket's 12% Democratic price and the absence of any Democratic-leaning evidence support only a modest chance of an upset.", "watch": "A late Democratic surge in fundraising or outside spending, or a favorable national environment, could narrow the margin enough to move this toward Lean R.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Derek Schmidt (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Kansas' 2nd District is a Republican-leaning seat where first-term Representative Derek Schmidt is seeking reelection. He won his primary handily in August and holds a clear financial advantage over Democrat Don Coover, with roughly $939,000 on hand compared to Coover's $244,000. No third-party or independent spending has been reported in the race.\n\nEvery major expert rater places the seat in the Safe, Solid, or Likely Republican column, and prediction markets give Democrats only about a one-in-eight chance. With no general-election polling available, the forecast rests on the district's strong partisan lean, Schmidt's incumbency advantage, and the consensus of professional ratings, all of which point to a comfortable Republican win.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0506, "margin": -10.48}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0308, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0524, "margin": -12.0}]}